cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite both the paper and the software."
title: "Companion code for 'From Hand-Crafted to LLM-Based Variation Operators in Metaheuristics: A Tutorial'"
abstract: >-
  Runnable reference implementation accompanying the tutorial "From Hand-Crafted to
  LLM-Based Variation Operators in Metaheuristics." Includes the build-and-validate
  loop (Algorithm 1) in Python and in C++, a transient solution-level operator (TSP),
  an amortized code-emitting operator (online bin packing), the drop-channel
  ablation, and five notebooks that walk through them. Everything runs offline via a
  deterministic mock model; the two implementations of the loop are checked against
  the same frozen output.
type: software
